-| Placement | Put each job in the tool that owns it (git hook, CLI, script): one job per module, few links between modules, the simplest form that works. A harness extension needs a reason: the job lives inside the harness (stream, compaction, rendering, in-loop retry) or no tool can see it. No pi extension for git or file work a hook or script can do. | Deterministic, harness-agnostic, low coupling: the same behavior under pi, Claude Code and a bare shell. The rule is in `agents-md/standards.md`, so every harness built from the fragments carries it. |
-| Scout git guard | `bin/guard/git` is first on PATH in every scout child, read and `--rw`. It blocks push, pull, merge, rebase, reset, clean, stash, checkout, switch and restore (plus commit and add for read scouts), only against the scout's own repo; exit 1 is a refused command, exit 77 means the guard is misconfigured (no real git) and nothing can run. | A token scan misses wrapper spellings; PATH catches every call of `git` by name. A tripwire, not a sandbox: an absolute `/usr/bin/git` or `git -c alias.x=...` gets past. |
-| Auto-run git hooks | `config/git/bin/auto-guard` runs from `init.templateDir` stubs (new repos, `home/.gitconfig`), from one line `git-hooks-install` inserts into existing sh/bash hooks, from husky's `~/.config/husky/init.sh`, and from dotfiles' `githooks/`. While a root `AUTO.md` exists it refuses commits and merge commits on the default branch and every push; otherwise it is silent. | Git enforces it under any harness. `--no-verify`, fast-forward merges and `update-ref` pass, so it is a tripwire. |
-| Worktrees | Branches come first; worktrees only when two trees must be live (the git-patterns skill says so). worktrunk (`wt`) copies every gitignored file (reflinked) with global excludes and no include list, since `.worktreeinclude` would put a new dotfile in every repo. `config/git/bin/worktree-setup` runs from post-checkout and wt's post-start (first wins) and installs only when a lockfile differs from main's. Main is primary for env files and `worktree-setup sync` pushes them (main wins); no symlinks. | One copy path for npm and pnpm repos, near-zero disk on APFS, and agents never edit env files. |
+## Harness
 
-## File layout
+- Single agent, soft modes as prompt templates: `/plan`, `/review`, `/memory`, `/challenge`, `/grill`, `/diagnose`, `/handoff`.
+- Put each job in the tool that owns it (git hook, CLI, script). A pi extension needs a job that lives inside the harness: stream, compaction, rendering, in-loop retry.
+- `bin/scout`: child `pi -p` with `read,grep,find,ls,bash`, no AGENTS.md, ~3.5k resident tokens, at most two live (exit 75), nesting refused, `bin/guard/git` first on PATH refusing history, remote, tree-switching, commit and add on the scout's repo.
+- `extensions/compact-cap.ts`: flat 210k cap checked when a run settles; a warning at 80%; compaction past the cap; never aborts a run. `prime-reminder.ts` points back at the rules after any compaction and resumes nothing.
+- `extensions/background.ts`: `bg_run` jobs, bash timeouts, a zero-token watchdog. `stream-watchdog.ts` aborts a silent model stream.
+- Prompt cache: `PI_CACHE_RETENTION=long` in `home/.zshrc` asks Anthropic for the 1h cache TTL.
+- Git hooks: `githooks/pre-commit` runs `build-agents.sh --check` in this repo; `config/git/template` stubs run `worktree-setup` in new repos.
 
